-- Q11833: Not-for-Profit Accounting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 958-210, an NFP reports its assets, liabilities, and net assets on the statement of financial position. This serves the same purpose as the for-profit balance sheet but uses NFP-specific terminology.
Wrong (B): "Statement of net assets" is not the standard title prescribed by FASB for private NFP financial statements.
Wrong (C): "Statement of net position" is a governmental accounting term under GASB, not applicable to private NFPs under FASB.
Wrong (D): The statement of activities reports revenues, expenses, and changes in net assets — it is the NFP equivalent of an income statement, not a balance sheet.$EXPL$
