  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 958-205-45-1, board-designated or quasi-endowment funds are classified as net assets without donor restrictions because the restriction is internally imposed. The board can reverse its own designation at any time without external approval.
Wrong (A): Board designations are not irrevocable; only donor-imposed restrictions require donor consent or legal action to reverse.
Wrong (C): Donor approval is irrelevant because the restriction was created by the board, not by an external donor.
Wrong (D): Board-designated funds were never classified as net assets with donor restrictions, so no reclassification between categories is needed.$EXPL$
