-- Q11837: Not-for-Profit Accounting [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 958-810-15, an NFP must consolidate another NFP when it has a controlling financial interest, demonstrated by majority board appointment and direction of strategic decisions. Cornerstone meets this for the physician group and research foundation.
Wrong (A): Mission alignment alone does not trigger consolidation; the Hospital Auxiliary is independently governed, so Cornerstone lacks control over it.
Wrong (C): The Auxiliary donates resources to Cornerstone, but an economic interest without control does not meet the consolidation threshold under ASC 958-810.
Wrong (D): NFPs are required to consolidate entities over which they have a controlling financial interest; the notion that NFPs never consolidate is incorrect.$EXPL$
